# Color — UI Palette Tokens

**ALWAYS** use `src/utils/color.ts` with **exact color name** variables (`ColorBlack`, `ColorWhite`, `ColorCream`…).

No role aliases (`ColorBg` / `ColorText` / `ColorLogo`). Three.js → `src/components/threejs/threeJSColors.ts`.

Together with `goldenRatio.ts` (space/size) and `typo.ts` (type), this is the project design system.

## Hard rules

1. **ALWAYS** import exact `Color*` names from `@/utils/color` — never paste `#E8E2DB` / `#000000` into className when a token exists.
2. When the user gives a **new UI color** (hex / name) → **update `color.ts` first** (exact `Color*` name + `colorCssVars` if needed), then wire UI.
3. Match an existing `Color*` when the hex already exists; otherwise add the token before using it in components.
4. Non-token hex **only** when the user explicitly overrides in chat.
5. New Three.js effect colors → update `threeJSColors.ts` first (`ThreeColor*`), not `color.ts`.

```ts
import { ColorBlack, ColorCream, ColorWhite } from '@/utils/color';

// ✅
style={{ backgroundColor: ColorBlack, color: ColorCream }}
style={{ color: ColorWhite }}

// ❌ role aliases
import { ColorBg, ColorText, ColorLogo } from '@/utils/color';

// ❌
className="bg-[#000000] text-[#E8E2DB]"
```

